    "introduction": "Associated British Foods combines the Primark clothing retailer with businesses in grocery products, ingredients, sugar and agriculture. Primark sells fashion and household products through a value-focused store network, while the food businesses supply consumers and commercial customers with branded groceries, baking ingredients and other products. Revenue is therefore spread across activities with different customers and economic drivers. Clothing demand and store productivity matter to retail, while crop conditions, commodity inputs and industrial demand influence food and agriculture. The group's decentralised structure allows its businesses to operate in specialised markets, supported by shared capital allocation and a portfolio that spans both consumer and business spending.",
